14  Tribunal should consider and decide with reference to  the evidence:
 (i) whether the disablement is permanent or  temporary;
 (ii) if the disablement is permanent, whether it is  permanent total disablement or permanent partial  disablement;
 (iii) if the disablement percentage is expressed with  reference to any specific limb, then the effect of such  disablement of the limb on the functioning of the  entire body, that is, the permanent disability suffered  by the person.
MACT No. 728/2017 Akhlak Ali vs. Siddharth @ Kishan Page No. 19 of 32  If the Tribunal concludes that there is no permanent  disability then there is no question of proceeding  further and determining the loss of future earning  capacity.
